      const cur = DATA.climate.ytd; $('#l12TrigN', root).innerHTML = `${G('A')} DFW Airport daily records aggregated by month in the atlas weather file. Read the odds as planning rules: a June flight has a coin flip's chance of a 100°F day and near certainty of 95°F; July and August carry ${D(C.m100[6], 0)} and ${D(C.m100[7], 0)} hundred degree days on average; the first 100°F day arrived in June or July in ${P((first[5] + first[6]) / fTot * 100, 0)} of seasons. Hard freezes (20°F) are a January phenomenon (${P(C.pfr20[0], 0)}) with December and February close behind. ${String(cur.through).slice(0, 4)} has already logged ${cur.d100} days at 100°F against a normal of ${cur.norm_d100}. Large hail: the 25 biggest reports in the file, by month.`;
